## Before your first apply

1. **Enable API access** for the account at
   [porkbun.com/account/api](https://porkbun.com/account/api), then opt in per
   domain, or globally with "Opt In All Domains". An API key cannot operate on
   a domain that has not opted in, however well scoped it is. The
   `porkbun_domains` data source filtered on `api_access = true` verifies this
   for free before a wide apply.
2. **Check DNSSEC.** If a DS record exists at the registry and the new
   nameservers do not serve the matching signed zone, every validating
   resolver returns SERVFAIL the moment the delegation changes. This is the
   only failure mode here that takes a domain completely dark rather than
   merely stale.
3. **Avoid an IP allowlist on the API key** — CI runner addresses are not
   stable, and the result is `IP_NOT_ALLOWED`. Scope the key by domain.

## Authentication

Credentials come from the provider configuration, or from the
`PORKBUN_API_KEY` and `PORKBUN_SECRET_KEY` environment variables. They are
sent as `X-API-Key` and `X-Secret-API-Key` headers, never in a request body.

From an IPv6-only network, set `base_url` to
`https://api-ipv4.porkbun.com/api/json/v3`.

